WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.120 --> 00:00:01.860
- [Reporter] The morning of October 9th,

00:00:01.860 --> 00:00:03.360
fragments of a Hamas missile

00:00:03.360 --> 00:00:06.360
land less than a mile outside
of Ben Gurion Airport,

00:00:06.360 --> 00:00:08.453
Israel's main international airport.

00:00:08.453 --> 00:00:09.286
(passengers shouting)

00:00:09.286 --> 00:00:11.457
On the ground, passengers ran for cover.

00:00:11.457 --> 00:00:12.510
(passengers shouting)

00:00:12.510 --> 00:00:13.650
In the skies above,

00:00:13.650 --> 00:00:16.440
A Ryanair flight on
approach diverted away.

00:00:16.440 --> 00:00:17.760
And yet, in a matter of minutes,

00:00:17.760 --> 00:00:20.850
aircraft resumed taking off
and landing at the airport,

00:00:20.850 --> 00:00:22.440
while the war continued.

00:00:22.440 --> 00:00:24.300
Despite it being less than 40 miles

00:00:24.300 --> 00:00:27.000
from the front lines of
Israel's war with Gaza,

00:00:27.000 --> 00:00:29.190
Ben Gurion airport has remained open

00:00:29.190 --> 00:00:30.480
throughout the conflict.

00:00:30.480 --> 00:00:33.750
And while civil air spaces
above war zones, like Ukraine,

00:00:33.750 --> 00:00:36.600
often remain closed from
the moment war breaks out,

00:00:36.600 --> 00:00:38.670
Israel's civil airspace has continued

00:00:38.670 --> 00:00:40.380
to receive commercial traffic.

00:00:40.380 --> 00:00:43.440
- I think the key question
here that everyone's asking is

00:00:43.440 --> 00:00:46.080
why haven't the Israelis
closed their airspace?

00:00:46.080 --> 00:00:49.200
And I think the answer is
countries are always going to err

00:00:49.200 --> 00:00:50.670
on the side of keeping it open.

00:00:50.670 --> 00:00:53.220
- [Reporter] So how does
Israel keep an airport open

00:00:53.220 --> 00:00:54.210
in a warzone?

00:00:54.210 --> 00:00:56.853
And what are the risks to
aircraft in the airspace?

00:00:58.470 --> 00:01:01.200
Keeping airspace open can
provide a vital corridor

00:01:01.200 --> 00:01:04.410
for Israel to allow people
to leave, soldiers to return,

00:01:04.410 --> 00:01:07.050
and goods and supplies to
continue entering the country

00:01:07.050 --> 00:01:08.400
during the conflict.

00:01:08.400 --> 00:01:10.230
One of the steps the country has taken

00:01:10.230 --> 00:01:12.120
to try and protect those aircraft

00:01:12.120 --> 00:01:15.240
is to change the route they're
approaching Ben Gurion from.

00:01:15.240 --> 00:01:18.000
- The main mitigation
measure that we've taken

00:01:18.000 --> 00:01:21.180
is completely separating the routes

00:01:21.180 --> 00:01:23.040
from the area of the conflict.

00:01:23.040 --> 00:01:25.620
The routes, basically,
in and out of Israel

00:01:25.620 --> 00:01:28.740
are much northern than they are usually,

00:01:28.740 --> 00:01:30.900
going 10 miles south of Haifa.

00:01:30.900 --> 00:01:33.390
- [Reporter] According to
Israel's Civil Aviation Authority,

00:01:33.390 --> 00:01:36.030
the country's civil and
military air traffic controllers

00:01:36.030 --> 00:01:38.010
also work very closely together

00:01:38.010 --> 00:01:39.870
and often sit in the same buildings

00:01:39.870 --> 00:01:41.965
and look at the same aerial picture.

00:01:41.965 --> 00:01:42.930
(missile fires)

00:01:42.930 --> 00:01:44.490
And that allows them to coordinate

00:01:44.490 --> 00:01:45.990
on trying to ensure that missiles

00:01:45.990 --> 00:01:47.970
from the country's Iron Dome system

00:01:47.970 --> 00:01:49.680
don't impact civilian aircraft

00:01:49.680 --> 00:01:51.600
when they're intercepting Hamas missile.

00:01:51.600 --> 00:01:53.820
- It still leaves plenty of flexibility

00:01:53.820 --> 00:01:57.450
for the defense systems
to plan their engagement,

00:01:57.450 --> 00:02:00.750
to plan their interception of a rocket.

00:02:00.750 --> 00:02:01.583
- [Reporter] On the ground,

00:02:01.583 --> 00:02:03.300
while Ben Gurion in
airport can normally have

00:02:03.300 --> 00:02:05.400
over 10 aircraft waiting at its gates...

00:02:05.400 --> 00:02:07.350
- We've limited the number of aircraft

00:02:07.350 --> 00:02:10.560
that are loaded with
passengers and with fuel,

00:02:10.560 --> 00:02:13.560
so you would see maximum
six, normally four.

00:02:13.560 --> 00:02:15.300
- [Reporter] And when the
aircraft are ready to depart,

00:02:15.300 --> 00:02:17.250
takeoff is as swift as possible,

00:02:17.250 --> 00:02:18.810
with no queuing on the runway.

00:02:18.810 --> 00:02:20.400
Israel's Civil Aviation Authority

00:02:20.400 --> 00:02:21.600
says that part of the reason

00:02:21.600 --> 00:02:23.610
it's able to keep its airspace open

00:02:23.610 --> 00:02:26.040
is because it has
remained open previously,

00:02:26.040 --> 00:02:28.410
through years of Hamas missile attacks.

00:02:28.410 --> 00:02:30.960
- So no one is doing anything new.

00:02:30.960 --> 00:02:33.810
Civil Aviation doesn't
like doing new stuff,

00:02:33.810 --> 00:02:36.330
not in general, and
specifically not in conflict.

00:02:36.330 --> 00:02:37.260
- [Reporter] And that's why the country

00:02:37.260 --> 00:02:38.640
issued a notice to airlines,

00:02:38.640 --> 00:02:40.740
saying its airspace would remain open

00:02:40.740 --> 00:02:42.750
but that airlines should use caution,

00:02:42.750 --> 00:02:46.230
a notice the FAA and EASA,
its European equivalent,

00:02:46.230 --> 00:02:47.790
have also sent out.

00:02:47.790 --> 00:02:51.300
Yet, despite this, the vast
bulk of international carriers

00:02:51.300 --> 00:02:53.340
have paused flying to Tel Aviv.

00:02:53.340 --> 00:02:55.440
While many airlines
stopped flying to Tel Aviv

00:02:55.440 --> 00:02:57.870
the day Hamas launched
its surprise attack,

00:02:57.870 --> 00:03:00.390
others continued to to
fly for a few days more.

00:03:00.390 --> 00:03:02.670
A British Airways flight
actually turned back

00:03:02.670 --> 00:03:04.170
moments before landing,

00:03:04.170 --> 00:03:05.820
as air raid sirens were sounding

00:03:05.820 --> 00:03:07.470
in the area surrounding the airport.

00:03:07.470 --> 00:03:09.510
- [Pilot] British Airways
has issued a statement,

00:03:09.510 --> 00:03:11.819
saying it's suspended
all flights to Tel Aviv

00:03:11.819 --> 00:03:12.870
until further notice.

00:03:12.870 --> 00:03:16.110
- Some Arnos, even though
their insurance allows

00:03:16.110 --> 00:03:18.660
these operations, they don't want it.

00:03:18.660 --> 00:03:21.120
Again, understandable.

00:03:21.120 --> 00:03:22.860
- [Reporter] Even though
the airspace remains open,

00:03:22.860 --> 00:03:25.260
airlines will have many
questions to consider

00:03:25.260 --> 00:03:27.210
if they operate flights into the region.

00:03:27.210 --> 00:03:30.660
- How frequent is the
rocket fire from Gaza?

00:03:30.660 --> 00:03:34.530
How deep into Israel are
Rockets being launched?

00:03:34.530 --> 00:03:37.740
Where are those Iron Dome
intercepts taking place?

00:03:37.740 --> 00:03:39.720
- [Narrator] Matt Borie is
Chief Intelligence Officer

00:03:39.720 --> 00:03:42.660
and one of the co-founders
of Osprey Flight Solutions,

00:03:42.660 --> 00:03:44.520
an aviation risk management company

00:03:44.520 --> 00:03:47.160
that advises the likes of America's TSA.

00:03:47.160 --> 00:03:50.250
His job is to evaluate some
of the worst-case scenarios,

00:03:50.250 --> 00:03:52.230
and he thinks that Israel's airspace

00:03:52.230 --> 00:03:53.700
should be more restricted.

00:03:53.700 --> 00:03:55.860
- The area where the
conflict is affecting,

00:03:55.860 --> 00:04:00.600
which includes Northern
Israel, Haifa, Tel Aviv,

00:04:00.600 --> 00:04:04.050
should be paused until the trajectory

00:04:04.050 --> 00:04:05.970
of this conflict becomes more clear.

00:04:05.970 --> 00:04:06.900
- [Reporter] Matt cautioned that,

00:04:06.900 --> 00:04:08.580
even though aircraft were being rerouted

00:04:08.580 --> 00:04:09.900
to approach over Haifa,

00:04:09.900 --> 00:04:12.510
there had still been recent
surface-to-air missile,

00:04:12.510 --> 00:04:14.280
or SAM, activity in the region.

00:04:14.280 --> 00:04:15.930
- The IDF has confirmed they employed

00:04:15.930 --> 00:04:18.750
a conventional SAM system to
shoot down a rocket launch

00:04:18.750 --> 00:04:19.890
from Gaza, near Haifa.

00:04:19.890 --> 00:04:21.540
- [Reporter] Footage of
the impact later appeared

00:04:21.540 --> 00:04:22.410
on social media.

00:04:22.410 --> 00:04:24.090
- Why this is a concern

00:04:24.090 --> 00:04:26.070
is because now we're
creating the conditions

00:04:26.070 --> 00:04:27.030
for a shoot-down.

00:04:27.030 --> 00:04:30.750
Civil aviation flying in between areas

00:04:30.750 --> 00:04:32.940
where conflict activity is happening.

00:04:32.940 --> 00:04:34.860
- [Reporter] Israel says
that when a missile is fired,

00:04:34.860 --> 00:04:36.030
its air traffic controllers

00:04:36.030 --> 00:04:37.710
can have over a minute and a half

00:04:37.710 --> 00:04:39.840
to maneuver aircraft out of the area,

00:04:39.840 --> 00:04:42.840
and in that time, aircraft
can cover around 10 miles.

00:04:42.840 --> 00:04:44.400
While neither Hamas nor Israel

00:04:44.400 --> 00:04:47.490
is likely to intentionally
target civilian aircraft,

00:04:47.490 --> 00:04:49.140
according to Matt, there's still a risk

00:04:49.140 --> 00:04:51.240
that an aircraft could be shot down

00:04:51.240 --> 00:04:54.540
if it's misidentified as
a missile or other threat,

00:04:54.540 --> 00:04:55.770
which is exactly what happened

00:04:55.770 --> 00:04:57.840
when Malaysia Airlines Flight 17

00:04:57.840 --> 00:05:01.290
was shot down over eastern
Ukraine by pro-Russia militia.

00:05:01.290 --> 00:05:03.300
- Weather caused this aircraft

00:05:03.300 --> 00:05:05.550
to deviate from its flight path,

00:05:05.550 --> 00:05:08.610
which led to the rebel group

00:05:08.610 --> 00:05:11.310
to interpret it as not a civilian airliner

00:05:11.310 --> 00:05:14.850
because it wasn't flying on
the civilian airliner routes,

00:05:14.850 --> 00:05:18.270
so Osprey has already told its clients

00:05:18.270 --> 00:05:20.460
that we assess the potential

00:05:20.460 --> 00:05:23.940
for miscalculation or misidentification

00:05:23.940 --> 00:05:27.630
in Israeli airspace to be
likely in the near term

00:05:27.630 --> 00:05:28.980
under the current scenario.

00:05:28.980 --> 00:05:31.110
- [Reporter] Israel denies
that misidentification

00:05:31.110 --> 00:05:33.390
is a major risk factor in its airspace.

00:05:33.390 --> 00:05:35.190
- There are technical limitations

00:05:35.190 --> 00:05:38.130
on some of the systems that, again,

00:05:38.130 --> 00:05:41.610
there is no possibility
that an interceptor

00:05:41.610 --> 00:05:44.580
could target a civilian aircraft.

00:05:44.580 --> 00:05:48.813
If anyone has a minimal
knowledge in aviation,

00:05:49.770 --> 00:05:54.147
a screen showing a drone
and a civilian aircraft

00:05:54.147 --> 00:05:57.360
and a fighter jet looks
very, very different.

00:05:57.360 --> 00:06:01.680
And the MA-17 and other
tragic accidents that happened

00:06:01.680 --> 00:06:04.290
have a very, very different background,

00:06:04.290 --> 00:06:07.470
and none of it is
relevant in this conflict.

00:06:07.470 --> 00:06:08.640
- [Reporter] While the situation in Israel

00:06:08.640 --> 00:06:11.910
is already complex, the
addition of outside forces,

00:06:11.910 --> 00:06:14.910
like Syria and Hezbollah,
who have already engaged

00:06:14.910 --> 00:06:17.250
in limited artillery
exchanges with Israel,

00:06:17.250 --> 00:06:18.960
could complicate things further.

00:06:18.960 --> 00:06:21.930
- Do you trust Hezbollah
will not make a mistake

00:06:21.930 --> 00:06:24.480
on firing on a target
over northern Israel?

00:06:24.480 --> 00:06:25.380
- [Reporter] Israel, however,

00:06:25.380 --> 00:06:28.050
says that it is monitoring
risks from all sides.

00:06:28.050 --> 00:06:29.970
- We're monitoring very, very closely

00:06:29.970 --> 00:06:32.040
and looking at the risk very carefully,

00:06:32.040 --> 00:06:34.200
monitoring the situation in Lebanon,

00:06:34.200 --> 00:06:36.390
monitoring the situation in Syria.

00:06:36.390 --> 00:06:37.680
I can assure you that,

00:06:37.680 --> 00:06:40.650
if we see many rockets
launched towards Ben Gurion,

00:06:40.650 --> 00:06:42.510
we will freeze traffic in Ben Gurion,

00:06:42.510 --> 00:06:45.180
and traffic will go to Eilat Ramon.

00:06:45.180 --> 00:06:46.620
- [Reporter] As the situation in the skies

00:06:46.620 --> 00:06:50.010
above Israel evolves, its
aviation authority maintains

00:06:50.010 --> 00:06:52.950
that it will remain
accountable, whatever happens

00:06:52.950 --> 00:06:55.350
- We monitor the situation closely.

00:06:55.350 --> 00:06:56.700
We listen to intel.

00:06:56.700 --> 00:06:59.550
We see ourselves as accountable.

00:06:59.550 --> 00:07:03.086
And we look at this role
very, very seriously.

00:07:03.086 --> 00:07:05.669
(tense music)

